(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers."] [15 1 "// signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C"] [16 1 "// handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;"] [17 1 "// the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL"] [18 1 "// signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux."] [19 1 "// The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:"] [20 1 "// a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked."] [26 1 "// sysPidfdSendSignal is pidfd_send_signal's syscall number (424 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)"] [31 39 "// the main thread's wake-up from a blocking wait"] [32 39 "// any arrival (sigwait)"] [33 39 "// tripped, its handler to run"] [34 39 "// is_tripped"] [35 39 "// pthread_sigmask's mask"] [36 39 "// arrived while blocked (sigpending)"] [37 39 "// notified on sigCh"] [38 39 "// arrivals so far (pidfd_send_signal's wait)"] [39 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's fd, -1 none"] [41 2 "// sigHandlers are the Python-level handlers (Handlers[n].func), touched under the GIL"] [43 21 "// default_int_handler"] [48 1 "// startSignals starts the receiver once."] [61 1 "// ownSignalHook, when set, handles a signal pyi sends itself (killSignal of its own pid, raise_signal) before the"] [62 1 "// signal module does (queue 220: faulthandler's handlers, and the default action that ends the process): handled true"] [63 1 "// and the call returns."] [66 1 "// signalTakenHook, when set, says a signal's handler is another module's (queue 220: faulthandler.register without"] [67 1 "// chain replaces the Python handler, as its sigaction does): the Python handler is not tripped."] [70 1 "// deliverSignal is the C handler: held when blocked, else tripped; the wakeup fd written."] [90 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [101 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [102 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [133 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [134 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [161 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [162 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [163 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [180 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [194 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [213 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [214 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [234 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [235 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [280 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [402 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [425 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [534 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [538 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [591 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [662 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd